  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need or is in a sustainable location, and further would not provide an adequate quality of accommodation to support a high standard of living by means of the insufficient size of Bedrooms 3, 6, and particularly Bedroom 5. The development would result in a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers through an increase in disturbance and comings and goings. The site is therefore not suitable for an HMO use. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (December, 2024)Policies D6, D14 and T4 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The development fails to demonstrate that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore likely to add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DMT1 and DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
